 "notes": "Region and the specific first-vs-second NAT used by both private tables are not distinguishable (both NATs carry the same tag); pvt_rt*_via_nat accepts either NAT. Port checks require TCP rules, so an all-protocol rule does not stand in for a stated port. pvt_from_public_sg / pvt_egress_public_sg read the declared configuration (the planned security_groups source is unknown): an ingress (egress) entry or rule whose source is a security group and that references the public group; the inline egress branch also requires no CIDR destination. pvt_no_open_cidr's inline branch requires every ingress entry of the private group to have no CIDR source; when the group has no inline ingress (separate rule resources) the check cannot tell which group a rule belongs to and passes. Not expressible: 'SSH only from 203.0.113.0/24' and 'egress limited to the VPC CIDR' as negatives over separate rule resources (no 'no element matches' operator and no min-0 count); the inline branch of allow_egress_vpc does enforce every egress CIDR."
}